{"name":"Corkscrew Willow","hex":"#d1b9ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"corkscrew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An implement for opening bottles that are sealed by a cork. Sometimes specifically such an implement that includes a screw-shaped part, or worm.","The screw-shaped worm of a typical corkscrew."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the tightly winding shape of a corkscrew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/corkscrew"},{"term":"willow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous trees or shrubs in the genus Salix, in the willow family Salicaceae, found primarily on moist soils in cooler zones in the northern hemisphere.","The wood of these trees."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open and cleanse (cotton, flax, wool, etc.) by means of a willow.","To form a shape or move in a way similar to the long, slender branches of a willow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/willow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salix babylonica","blocks":[{"text":"Salix babylonica is a species of willow native to dry areas of northern China, Korea, Mongolia, Japan, and Siberia but cultivated for millennia elsewhere in Asia, being traded along the Silk Road to southwest Asia and Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Chenonceau_-_jardin_Russell-Page_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Chenonceau_-_jardin_Russell-Page_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salix_babylonica","wikidata":"Q156307"},{"title":"Corkscrew","blocks":[{"text":"A corkscrew is a tool for drawing corks from wine bottles and other household bottles that may be sealed with corks. In its traditional form, a corkscrew simply consists of a pointed metallic helix attached to a handle, which the user screws into the cork and pulls to extract it. Corkscrews are necessary because corks themselves, being small and smooth, are difficult to grip and remove, particularly when inserted fully into an inflexible glass bottle. More recent styles of corkscrew incorporate various systems of levers that further increase the amount of force that can be applied outwards upon the cork, making the extraction of difficult corks easier."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Corkscrews_December_2014-1.jpg/330px-Corkscrews_December_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corkscrew","wikidata":"Q12337"},{"title":"Willow","blocks":[{"text":"Willows, also called sallows and osiers, of the genus Salix, comprise around 350 species of typically deciduous trees and shrubs. They are primarily found on moist soils in cold and temperate regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow","wikidata":"Q36050"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg/120px-Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg/250px-Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg/120px-Saule_pleureur_chaton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaule_pleureur_chaton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Willow_Salix_babylonica.jpg/120px-Willow_Salix_babylonica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.